.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-APPLICATIONS 7
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-applications
.Nd how Wattle applications are laid out and installed
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An
.Em application
is a project that declares one or more executable programs under
.Ql ":exes"
for installation.
At least one executable must have type
.Ql ":native"
or
.Ql ":source" ;
web executables are not installed.
.Pp
This page describes how applications are installed,
where their files are placed and how application scripts customise
installation.
See
.Xr wattle-projects 7
for executable,
library and documentation declarations,
and
.Xr wattle-apps 1
for the commands that manage installed applications.
.
.Sh LAYOUT
An application has the layout of a Wattle project.
Its info file provides the information needed for installation,
and it may also include an
.Em application script
that defines installation hooks:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa ./info.edn
.Ec
.Xc
The info file,
located in the project root.
Installation requires the
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group"
keys.
See
.Sx "INFO FILE"
in
.Xr wattle-projects 7 .
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa hooks/init.wattle
.Ec
.Xc
The application script.
.Eo
.Pa ./hooks.wattle
.Ec
may be used instead.
If both files exist,
.Eo
.Pa hooks/init.wattle
.Ec
is used.
The rest of
.Eo
.Pa hooks/
.Ec
is installed with the script,
so it can use relative imports to load the files beside it.
.El
.Pp
An application requires
.Ql ":name"
and
.Ql ":group"
in its info file.
Both are single directory names:
neither may be empty,
.Ql "\&."
or
.Ql "\&.\&." ,
or contain a path separator.
The group is conventionally a reverse domain such as
.Ql "org\&.example" .
Installed application names are unique across groups.
.
.Sh INSTALLATION
Without an application script,
.Ql "wattle apps install"
installs the programs declared in the info file.
Each executable with
.Ql ":type :native"
or
.Ql ":type :source"
is installed with the libraries and documentation that name
it in
.Ql ":for" :
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n
.It
A native executable is built with
.Xr wattle-build 1
and installed in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec .
Its associated native libraries are linked into the program,
and its imported source libraries are compiled into the program.
.It
A source executable is installed as described in
.Sx "Source programs" .
.It
Each associated manual page is installed in
.Eo
.Pa share/man/
.Ec .
The digit at the end of the file name determines its manual
section.
.El
.Pp
A remote library is fetched under
.Eo
.Pa lib/wattle/.fetch/
.Ec
and installed as the source or native library declared in its
own info file.
The application’s
.Em manifest
records the installed files and source revisions.
Each remote library has an entry under
.Ql ":libs"
with its
.Ql ":name" ,
.Ql ":url"
and
.Ql ":rev" .
.Pp
Web executables are not installed.
A library or documentation declaration is not installed unless
its
.Ql ":for"
names an installed executable.
A web documentation declaration that names an installed executable
is an error.
.Pp
The manifest lists each file installed in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec
and
.Eo
.Pa share/man/
.Ec .
.Ql "wattle apps remove"
removes these files and the application directory.
.Pp
If the project includes an application script,
installation runs its hooks instead of installing from the declarations.
See
.Sx "Hooks" .
.
.Ss Source programs
A source executable is installed by copying the paths in its
.Ql ":files"
vector into the application directory.
When a directory is copied,
entries named
.Ql "zig-out" ,
.Ql "\&.zig-cache" ,
.Ql "\&.wattle"
or
.Ql "\&.git"
are excluded.
.Pp
Associated source libraries are placed in
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/
.Ec
in the application directory,
as described in
.Xr wattle-projects 7 .
Associated native libraries are built with
.Xr wattle-build 1
in the project and copied to
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/lib/
.Ec
in the application directory.
Building these modules requires
.Ic zig
on
.Ev PATH .
.Ql "wattle apps upgrade"
builds the modules again.
.Pp
Installation also creates a
.Em wrapper ,
a program in
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec
with the name of the executable.
The wrapper starts with
.Ql "#!/usr/bin/env wattle" .
It loads the file specified by
.Ql ":entry"
and calls
.Ql "main"
with the wrapper’s path followed by the command-line arguments.
.Pp
A bare import searches
.Eo
.Pa .wattle/
.Ec
and
.Eo
.Pa zig-out/lib/
.Ec
in the application directory.
Vendored source under
.Eo
.Pa deps/
.Ec
is imported by a relative path.
Running the installed program requires
.Ic wattle
on
.Ev PATH
and the prefix set with
.Ev WATTLE_PREFIX .
A native executable requires neither.
Source executables cannot be installed on Windows,
which has no shebang lines.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:name \(dqgreeter\(dq
 :group \(dqnet\&.inqk\(dq
 :exes \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqgreet\(dq
         :entry \(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq
         :files \(lB\(dqmain\&.wattle\(dq \(dqlib\(dq \(dqdeps\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :libs \(lB{:type :source
         :name \(dqutil\(dq
         :root \(dqutil\(dq
         :for \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB
 :docs \(lB{:type :man
         :files \(lB\(dqman/greet\&.1\(dq\(rB
         :for \(lB\(dqgreet\(dq\(rB}\(rB}
.Ed
.
.Ss Hooks
An application script replaces installation from the declarations
in
.Ql "info\&.edn" .
The installer also permits a project with an application script
and no
.Ql ":exes"
declarations.
This form of installation is discouraged.
Applications should declare their executable programs under
.Ql ":exes" ,
including when hooks perform the installation.
.Pp
A
.Em hook
is a function defined in the application script.
Each hook takes the application’s manifest as its argument.
Installation runs the hooks in this order:
.Pp
.Bl -enum -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "clean" ,
only when a clean build is requested
.It
.Ql "build"
.It
.Ql "install"
.It
.Ql "check" ,
only when a check is requested
.El
.Pp
The
.Ql "remove"
hook runs when the application is removed.
.Pp
Within a hook,
these functions add files to the manifest,
so that
.Ql "wattle apps remove"
can remove them:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql "app/add-bin"
.Xc
Adds a program to the directory for installed executables,
the
.Em binpath .
.It Xo
.Ql "app/add-manpage"
.Xc
Adds a manual page to the directory for installed manual pages,
the
.Em manpath .
.El
.Pp
Example of
.Eo
.Pa hooks/init.wattle
.Ec :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpdefn install
  \(lBmanifest &\(rB
  \*(lpapp/add-bin manifest \(dqhello\(dq\*(rp
  \*(lpapp/add-manpage manifest \(dqhello\&.1\(dq\*(rp\*(rp
.Ed
.
.Sh INSTALLED FILES
All locations are relative to the installation prefix,
.Ql "*prefix*" .
See
.Ev WATTLE_PREFIX
in
.Xr wattle 1 .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa lib/wattle/
.Ec
.Xc
The directory for installed applications,
the
.Em libpath .
.Ql "import"
does not search this directory.
See
.Sx "MODULES"
in
.Xr wattle 7 .
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa lib/wattle/apps/<group>/<name>/
.Ec
.Xc
The directory for an individual application.
It contains
.Ql "manifest\&.edn" ,
a copy of the info file and,
when present,
the application script and the rest of
.Eo
.Pa hooks/
.Ec .
Source programs and their libraries are also copied here.
.Pp
The manifest records the application’s source and its revision
under
.Ql ":rev" ,
and the revision of each remote library under
.Ql ":libs" .
A Git revision is a commit hash.
A tarball or directory revision is
.Ql "sha256:"
followed by a hash of its files.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa bin/
.Ec
.Xc
The binpath,
containing installed native executables and source wrappers.
.It Xo
.Eo
.Pa share/man/
.Ec
.Xc
The manpath,
containing manual pages in subdirectories such as
.Eo
.Pa man1/
.Ec .
.El
.
